From 3add1a7c18b382171f1ad18b1a120e1207af5540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video][Database] Repair versions turned into extras by
 upgrades < v131

Migration steps 123 to 131 were written for the itemType values of their
time (version 0, extra 1) but use the values introduced in v134, so
upgrading a database from before v131 turns movie versions and their
types into extras and empties the movie library.

Leave those steps unchanged and repair the damage in a new step, chosen
by the version the database started at. The repair also restores
databases already damaged by earlier builds.

Master runs the same repair as its v154 and adds the v150 column of
master that Kodi 22 v150 databases lack.

Fixes #29918

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
